      title: 'Digital and nonlinear control',
      summary: String.raw`Controllers today run on computers, which sample, compute and hold; discretisation methods translate continuous designs into code, and sampling brings its own delays and opportunities such as deadbeat control. Many plants are strongly nonlinear, and methods such as feedback linearisation, sliding modes, gain scheduling and adaptive control extend the linear toolkit to them, each with its own price in modelling effort or robustness.`,
